 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Try using a good webcam, and see if you can get it to work in full resolution. If not, your next step is to buy a cheap webcam. Shoot in wide mode, turn on the light with the window, and keep a small gap between the window and the shot. Roughly how much light are we talking about? Try to speak as clearly as possible, and see if you can close the window a bit. You can use sound software to reduce the echo, but it's much easier if you don't need it. Shoot at eye level, and try to keep the background simple. A plain wall in bright light is the least likely to cause problems.",
